  "reason": "The current best configuration (config_038: multimodal, multiprofile, scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, transformer, concat) achieves 0.721 accuracy. All multimodal results so far use 'concat' fusion; the 'weighted' fusion option is completely untested, leaving a key design dimension with zero evidence. Config_039 is identical to config_038 except fusion changes from concat to weighted, providing a clean one-variable comparison that isolates the fusion mechanism. In rna_only, aggregation (avgpool vs transformer) showed negligible difference (~0.003), suggesting that how features are combined (fusion) may be a more impactful unexplored axis than aggregation. Under a limited budget, testing weighted fusion directly against the current best tells us whether the simple concatenation is suboptimal or whether the multimodal signal is already well-captured, reducing uncertainty about a core architectural choice before committing further experiments to the concat paradigm."
